Let $D$ be the determinant of the given matrix. We have
\[ D = \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix}. \]Expanding along the first row gives
\begin{align*} D &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x \left( \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x \right) - \left( \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \right) + \left( \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \right) \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \right) - \frac{\cos^2 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \right) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1 - \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \end{align*}
An alternative method is to use the identity
\begin{align*} \sec^2 x - \cot^2 x &= 1 \\ \cos^2 x - \sin^2 x &= \cos 2x \end{align*}
Let $x = \frac{\pi}{4}$. Then $\sec^2 \frac{\pi}{4} = 2$, $\cos^2 \frac{\pi}{4} = \frac{1}{2}$, $\csc^2 \frac{\pi}{4} = \sqrt{2}$, $\cot^2 \frac{\pi}{4} = 1$.
\[ D = \begin{vmatrix} 2 & 1 & 1 \\ \frac{1}{2} & \frac{1}{2} & \sqrt{2} \\ 1 & \frac{1}{2} & 1 \end{vmatrix} \]
Expanding along the first row gives
\[ D = 2 \begin{vmatrix} \frac{1}{2} & \sqrt{2} \\ \frac{1}{2} & 1 \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \frac{1}{2} & \sqrt{2} \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \frac{1}{2} & \frac{1}{2} \\ 1 & \frac{1}{2} \end{vmatrix} \]
\[ = 2 \left( \frac{1}{2} - \sqrt{2} \cdot \frac{1}{2} \right) - \left( \frac{1}{2} - \sqrt{2} \right) + \left( \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{4} \right) \]
\[ = 2 \cdot \frac{1}{2} - \sqrt{2} - \frac{1}{2} + \sqrt{2} + 0 = 1 - \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{2} \]
Then $D = \frac{1}{2}$.

