Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be even functions. This means that $f(-x) = f(x)$ and $g(-x) = g(x)$ for all $x$. We want to determine if $f(x)g(x)$ is even, odd, or neither.
We need to find $f(-x)g(-x)$.
Since $f(x)$ is even, $f(-x) = f(x)$.
Since $g(x)$ is even, $g(-x) = g(x)$.
Therefore, $f(-x)g(-x) = f(x)g(x)$.
Since $f(-x)g(-x) = f(x)g(x)$, we have that $f(x)g(x)$ is an even function.

