Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be even functions. We want to determine if $h(x) = f(x)g(x)$ is even, odd, or neither.
We have $h(-x) = f(-x)g(-x)$.
Since $f(x)$ is even, $f(-x) = f(x)$.
Since $g(x)$ is even, $g(-x) = g(x)$.
Therefore, $h(-x) = f(-x)g(-x) = f(x)g(x) = h(x)$.
Since $h(-x) = h(x)$, $h(x) = f(x)g(x)$ is an even function.

