The total miles run by girls in $x$ days is $3 + 6(x-1)$ miles.
The total miles run by boys in $x$ days is $5x$ miles.
The average miles run by girls is $\frac{3 + 6(x-1)}{x}$ miles.
The average miles run by boys is $\frac{5x}{x} = 5$ miles.
We want to find $x$ such that $\frac{3 + 6(x-1)}{x} > 5$.
$3 + 6x - 6 > 5x$
$6x - 3 > 5x$
$x > 3$
The smallest integer greater than 3 is 4. Thus, $x=4$.
The total miles run by each girl is $3 + 6(4-1) = 3 + 6(3) = 3 + 18 = 21$.
The total miles run by each boy is $5(4) = 20$.
We want to find the total miles each girl has run by the time the coach orders the new equipment.
Since $x=4$, each girl has run 21 miles.

