We are given that the height $h = 6$ cm.  Substituting this into the equation $rh = 24$, we get $r(6) = 24$, so $r = \frac{24}{6} = 4$ cm.

The volume $V$ of a cylinder is given by $V = \pi r^2 h$.
Substituting $r = 4$ and $h = 6$, we get $V = \pi (4^2)(6) = \pi (16)(6) = 96\pi$ cubic centimeters.

